.Dd November 10, 2026
.Dt RACH2-GAME 1
.Os Rach2
.Sh NAME
.Nm rach2-game
.Nd run a Windows game through Proton and WineD3D on OpenGL
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -umu
.Op Fl -id Ar id
.Op Fl -prefix Ar directory
.Op Fl -print
.Op Fl -
.Op Ar program Op Ar argument ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
runs
.Ar program
through the x86-64 GNU root's GE-Proton11-12 at
.Pa /opt/proton/proton .
It uses WoW64 and WineD3D's OpenGL renderer with fsync enabled.
Steam is not required.
The program's arguments and exit status pass through Proton.
.Pp
.Fl -id
chooses a decimal game ID.
The default is the inherited
.Ev SteamGameId ,
or 0.
Give each game its own ID or compatibility directory.
.Fl -prefix
chooses that directory; Proton keeps the Wine prefix in its
.Pa pfx
child.
It takes precedence over
.Ev STEAM_COMPAT_DATA_PATH .
With neither, the directory is
.Pa $XDG_DATA_HOME/rach2/games/ID
or
.Pa $HOME/.local/share/rach2/games/ID .
All directory paths must be absolute.
.Pp
When the compatibility directory has no
.Pa pfx/user.reg ,
.Nm
first makes the prefix: it runs
.Li wineboot -u
through Proton and prints
.Dl rach2-game: prefix: made DIR
on standard error before it starts the program.
WineD3D takes the video memory from the GL driver, as under Linux.
.Pp
.Fl -print
prints the effective settings, one
.Ar NAME=value
per line, without creating directories or starting Proton.
No program is needed in this mode.
.Fl -help
prints usage.
.Fl -
ends option processing.
.Ss umu
.Fl -umu
runs Proton through
.Xr umu-run 1 ,
in the container of the pinned Steam Linux Runtime 4.0, steamrt4, as games
run outside Steam under Linux.
The settings and the prefix are the direct route's.
umu takes the compatibility directory as
.Ev WINEPREFIX
and links its
.Pa pfx
to the directory itself unless
.Pa pfx
is already a directory, as in one the direct route made.
.Pp
umu keeps the runtime in
.Pa $XDG_DATA_HOME/umu/steamrt4
or
.Pa $HOME/.local/share/umu/steamrt4 .
When that copy's
.Pa VERSIONS.txt
differs from
.Pa /opt/umu/VERSIONS.txt ,
or it has none,
.Nm
unpacks
.Pa /opt/umu/SteamLinuxRuntime_4.tar.xz
there, under umu's lock
.Pa umu.lock
beside it, replacing the old copy, and prints
.Dl rach2-game: umu: unpacked the Steam Linux Runtime VERSION in DIR
on standard error.
The copy takes 711 MB.
umu checks it with
.Nm pv-verify
on the first start and downloads nothing; with
.Ev UMU_RUNTIME_UPDATE
set to 0 it does not update the runtime either.
.Ss Crysis
The x86-64 GNU root also provides
.Nm crysis.sh .
An administrator first mounts the data partition writable at
.Pa /data
and creates
.Pa /data/crysis
owned by the user who will play.
As that user, run:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
crysis.sh install '/data/installers/setup_crysis_2.0.0.7_(84418).exe'
crysis.sh verify
crysis.sh run
.Ed
.Pp
Keep the installer's two
.Pa .bin
files beside its executable.
The installer checks their SHA-256 hashes, unpacks with
.Xr innoextract 1 ,
and checks all 2,358 game files against the system's manifest before
publishing
.Pa /data/crysis/game .
An existing game tree is refused; use
.Cm verify
to check it again.
.Pp
.Cm run
.Op Fl -umu
.Op Fl -32
.Op Fl -prefix Ar dir
starts
.Pa Bin64/Crysis.exe
with
.Fl dx9
from its own directory through
.Nm rach2-game
with game ID 17300.
.Fl -umu
starts it through umu instead, with
.Pa /data/crysis/game
as
.Ev STEAM_COMPAT_INSTALL_PATH ,
since the game finds no language from the root of the drive umu maps there,
and
.Pa /data
added to
.Ev PRESSURE_VESSEL_FILESYSTEMS_RW .
.Fl -32
starts the 32-bit
.Pa Bin32/Crysis.exe
under WoW64.
.Fl -prefix
chooses another compatibility directory under
.Pa /data ,
which the launcher makes on its first use, as a new player's would be.
Additional arguments follow these settings.
The game's
.Fl userpath
is
.Pa Z:\edata\ecrysis\esaves ;
its compatibility directory, logs, Steam client directory and Mesa cache
are respectively
.Pa /data/crysis/compat ,
.Pa /data/crysis/logs ,
.Pa /data/crysis/steam
and
.Pa /data/crysis/cache/mesa .
Mesa's on-disk cache is enabled.
With
.Ev MESA_SHADER_CACHE_SHOW_STATS=true
Mesa prints the cache's hits and misses only when it destroys the cache,
which Crysis's exit through Wine has not done.
These files and the saves survive an update of the system's root.
The game tree needs write access too, for its own logs.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Nm
sets these variables for Proton:
.Bl -tag -width STEAM_COMPAT_CLIENT_INSTALL_PATH
.It Ev PROTON_USE_WOW64
1, selecting Wine's WoW64 mode.
.It Ev PROTON_USE_WINED3D
1, selecting WineD3D instead of DXVK and vkd3d-proton.
.It Ev WINE_D3D_CONFIG
.Li renderer=gl ,
selecting OpenGL.
.It Ev PROTON_NO_FSYNC
0; Proton enables fsync and Wine checks the kernel's futex support.
.It Ev SteamGameId , SteamAppId
The chosen game ID.
.It Ev PROTON_LOG
1, enabling Proton's log and DLL load records.
.El
.Pp
With
.Fl -umu
it also sets these for umu:
.Bl -tag -width UMU_RUNTIME_UPDATE
.It Ev PROTONPATH
.Pa /opt/proton .
.It Ev GAMEID
.Li umu- Ns Ar id ,
from which umu sets
.Ev SteamGameId
and
.Ev SteamAppId
to
.Ar id .
.It Ev WINEPREFIX
The compatibility directory.
.It Ev UMU_RUNTIME_UPDATE
0, turning the runtime's update off.
.El
.Fl -print
then also prints these and
.Ev UMU_RUNTIME ,
the runtime's directory.
umu sets
.Ev STEAM_COMPAT_CLIENT_INSTALL_PATH
to the empty string inside the container.
.Pp
.Ev PROTON_LOG_DIR
chooses the log directory; its default is
.Pa logs
in the compatibility directory.
Proton writes
.Pa steam-ID.log
there, replacing the preceding launch's log.
.Pp
.Ev PULSE_LATENCY_MSEC
is kept when set; otherwise it is 60, the milliseconds of sound that
libpulse asks PulseAudio to hold for each of Wine's streams, in place of
Wine's own 30.
.Pp
.Ev STEAM_COMPAT_CLIENT_INSTALL_PATH
is kept when set; otherwise it names
.Pa steam
under the default
.Pa rach2/games
directory.
The launcher creates this directory for Proton without installing Steam.
.Ev DISPLAY
and the desktop session's other variables pass through unchanged.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
Usage errors exit with status 2, as do the launcher's own errors before it
starts Proton: a root other than x86-64, a missing
.Pa /opt/proton/proton ,
a missing
.Nm umu-run
or a missing runtime archive with
.Fl -umu .
A failed
.Li wineboot
in a new prefix, a
.Li wineboot
that leaves no
.Pa pfx/user.reg ,
or a failed unpacking of the runtime, exits with status 1.
Otherwise the exit status is Proton's, or umu's with
.Fl -umu .
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
rach2-game --id 17300 --prefix /data/crysis/compat /data/crysis/game/Bin64/Crysis.exe -dx9
rach2-game --umu --id 17300 --prefix /data/crysis/compat /data/crysis/game/Bin64/Crysis.exe -dx9
rach2-game --id 17300 --print
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr innoextract 1 ,
.Xr proton 1 ,
.Xr umu-run 1 ,
.Xr desktop 7
